# W9-T3 λ-estimator differential golden (deleted-interpolation EM parity
# with gen_deleted_ngram + estimate_interpolation).
#
# Configuration "X" (see docs/findings/lambda-port.md):
#   SYSTEM_BIGRAM + floored unigram  ← gen_ngram over fold A (first ⌊N/2⌋ =
#                                       116 lines of segmenter-ngseg.txt)
#   DELETED_BIGRAM (held-out)        ← gen_deleted_ngram over the full corpus
#   λ                                ← estimate_interpolation (seed 0.6,
#                                       ε 0.001, per-context EM, mean)
#
# The Rust estimator is fed the same integer counts (T2's counter over fold A
# for the system model, this crate's held-out counter over the full corpus)
# and reproduces λ bit-for-bit. `average_bits` is the IEEE-754 f64 bit
# pattern of the mean λ (a deterministic function of integer counts, so
# exact, not toleranced); `dump_fnv1a64` hashes the `token:%d lambda:%f` /
# `average lambda:%f` dump at six decimals — estimate_interpolation's own
# stdout shape. Against the live pin binaries the per-context λ are
# byte-identical at that six-decimal precision and the DELETED_BIGRAM counts
# are integer bit-exact; see the differential test.
contexts 153
system_bigrams 97
deleted_bigrams 199
uni_total 138202
average_bits 3fdc8629278cd1c5
average_decimal 0.44568852293312161
dump_fnv1a64 502672fce58909ae
